    {
      "title": "Apply verified corrections to general rules, not just specific log lines",
      "class": "FP-3a",
      "context": "When a verified correction updates a specific log entry by referencing a standing rule, the agent must apply that rule to all similar future cases, not just the corrected entry.",
      "observation": "The agent acknowledged the correction for a specific item but failed to apply the underlying rule (e.g., 'docent-guided visits are tours') to new, similar items in subsequent probes.",
      "lesson": "Treat verified corrections as updates to the general classification rule. Apply the corrected rule to all current and future items, not just the specific entry mentioned in the correction.",
      "applicability": [
        "A verified source provides a correction that references a standing rule or definition.",
        "The agent is asked to classify a new item that fits the corrected rule."
      ],
      "recommendedBehavior": "Extract the general rule from the correction. Apply this rule to the new query immediately, ignoring any prior incorrect classifications for similar items.",
